description: Module pattern — schema, component and query of a content module.
globs:
  - studio/schemas/objects/modules/**
  - web/src/components/modules/**
  - web/sanity/queries/components/modules/**
---

The wiring checklist (six points, inline opt-in) is in `AGENTS.md` §"The module pattern". Prefer `pnpm gen:module <Name>`; `pnpm check:wiring` compares every list.

- i18n: module fields are plain (`string`, `richText`, `richTextMedia`); the projection returns them as they are (the page query already selected the document's language) and the component renders them directly.
- File `module<Name>.ts`, `export const module<Name>` and `name: "module.<id>"` must match — `check:wiring` finds a module only by all three.
- Give every module schema a `preview`, or Studio lists each instance as "Untitled".
- Renaming `module.<id>` once content exists needs a data migration.
- Module components are server components. An interactive part goes behind a lazy client boundary like `web/src/components/media/LazyVideo.tsx` or `…/carousel/LazyCarouselViewport.tsx`, or it lands in every route's first-load JS.
